and CLI into a Docker image (WS-03). The initial Dockerfile was completed on 2026-06-16, but Diana's size/CVE review reopened the task on 2026-06-25 after the built image measured 2.1GB. Evan is redesigning the build as multi-stage toward a ~450MB target, swapped the base image to Alpine, and removed unused OCR and runtime packages that were not needed at runtime. As of the 2026-08-12 size/CVE verification, the image still exceeds the ~450MB target and CVE verification remains outstanding. This ClickUp record was opened at task creation; the reopening and remediation steps above were tracked through engineering channels.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-15\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-15\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-15\\n\\n**Title**: Docker Packaging\\n\\n**Status**: Active (Reopened)\\n\\n**Assignee**: Evan\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-06-11\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- Image size reduced to the ~450MB target (not yet met).\\n\\n- CVE verification passes with no outstanding findings (not yet met).\\n\\n- Task stays Active (Reopened) until both size and CVE checks pass.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-15\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-15\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-15\\n\\n**Title**: Docker Packaging\\n\\n**Status**: Active (Reopened)\\n\\n**Assignee**: Evan\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-06-11\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nContainerize CipherDoc's API and CLI into a Docker image (WS-03). The initial Dockerfile was completed on 2026-06-16, but Diana's size/CVE review reopened the task on 2026-06-25 after the built image measured 2.1GB. Evan is redesigning the build as multi-stage toward a ~450MB target, swapped the base image to Alpine, and removed unused OCR and runtime packages that were not needed at runtime. As of the 2026-08-12 size/CVE verification, the image still exceeds the ~450MB target and CVE verification remains outstanding. This ClickUp record was opened at task creation; the reopening and remediation steps above were tracked through engineering channels.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"clickup task ciph 15 sourc id src cu ciph 15 task id ciph 15 titl docker packag status activ reopen assigne evan prioriti normal date creat 2026 06 11 descript container cipherdoc s api and cli into a docker imag w 03 the initi dockerfil wa complet on 2026 06 16 but diana s size cve review reopen the task on 2026 06 25 after the built imag measur 2 1gb evan is redesign the build a multi stage toward a 450mb target swap the base imag to alpin and remov unus ocr and runtim packag that were not need at runtim a of the 2026 08 12 size cve verif the imag still exceed the 450mb target and cve verif remain outstand this clickup record wa open at task creation the reopen and remedi step abov were track through engin channel clickup task ciph 15 sourc id src cu ciph 15 task id ciph 15 titl docker packag status activ reopen assigne evan prioriti normal date creat 2026 06 11 accept criterion imag size reduc to the 450mb target not yet met cve verif pass with no outstand find not yet met task stay activ reopen until both size and cve check pas clickup task ciph 15 sourc id src cu ciph 15 task id ciph 15 titl docker packag status activ reopen assigne evan prioriti normal date creat 2026 06 11 descript container cipherdoc s api and cli into a docker imag w 03 the initi dockerfil wa complet on 2026 06 16 but diana s size cve review reopen the task on 2026 06 25 after the built imag measur 2 1gb evan is redesign the build a multi stage toward a 450mb target swap the base imag to alpin and remov unus ocr and runtim packag that were not need at runtim a of the 2026 08 12 size cve verif the imag still exceed the 450mb target and cve verif remain outstand this clickup record wa open at task creation the reopen and remedi step abov were track through engin channel\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"ee6a7df88a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-15-Docker-Packaging.md\", \"id\": \"461c66a96e55b847\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3392856173778035, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.16047126768257647, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7565191, \"dataset_name\": \"C1WR-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-15-Docker-Packaging.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"ee6a7df88a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-15-Docker-Packaging.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-15-Docker-Packaging.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1231, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:35:15\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:06:40\", \"token_count\": 678, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-03\\n\\n# Slack Thread: REST API Scaffolding and TempFile Policy\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-06-14\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-06-14 09:09] Bob**: Starting on the REST API scaffolding. Going with FastAPI for the layer. It's lightweight and the auto-generated OpenAPI docs will save us a ton of time.\\n\\n**[2026-06-14 09:39] Diana**: +1 for FastAPI. Can we ensure we have request validation schemas for the upload endpoint? We don't want malformed JSON crashing the engine.\\n\\n**[2026-06-14 09:43] Bob**: Already on it. Using Pydantic for the `RedactionRequest` model. Scaffold is up and running in the `api-scaffold` branch.\\n\\n**[2026-06-14 10:50] Bob**: Quick update on the file handling. I'm implementing a strict temp-file cleanup policy.\\n\\n**[2026-06-14 10:56] Diana**: How are we handling cleanup? If a request fails mid-stream, do we leave orphaned files on the container?\\n\\n**[2026-06-14 11:15] Bob**: No, I'm using a `try...finally` block with a context manager. Files are wiped immediately after the redaction job completes or errors out. No PII should ever persist in `/tmp`.\\n\\n**[2026-06-14 11:16] Diana**: What about memory-mapped files for larger uploads?\\n\\n**[2026-06-14 11:33] Bob**: For now, everything is streamed. We might need `mmap` later, but for the MVP, the context manager approach is safer.\\n\\n**[2026-06-14 11:47] Diana**: I'll start the security audit once you merge the policy. We need to be 100% sure about that cleanup logic.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 03 slack thread rest api scaffold and tempfil polici channel cipherdoc date 2026 06 14 2026 06 14 09 09 bob start on the rest api scaffold go with fastapi for the layer it s lightweight and the auto generat openapi doc will save u a ton of time 2026 06 14 09 39 diana 1 for fastapi can we ensur we have request valid schema for the upload endpoint we don t want malform json crash the engin 2026 06 14 09 43 bob alreadi on it use pydant for the redactionrequest model scaffold is up and run in the api scaffold branch 2026 06 14 10 50 bob quick updat on the file handl i m implement a strict temp file cleanup polici 2026 06 14 10 56 diana how are we handl cleanup if a request fail mid stream do we leav orphan file on the contain 2026 06 14 11 15 bob no i m use a tri final block with a context manag file are wipe immedi after the redact job complet or error out no pii should ever persist in tmp 2026 06 14 11 16 diana what about memori map file for larger upload 2026 06 14 11 33 bob for now everyth is stream we might need mmap later but for the mvp the context manag approach is safer 2026 06 14 11 47 diana i ll start the secur audit onc you merg the polici we need to be 100 sure about that cleanup logic\", \"dataset_id\": \"918880948a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"edecdf068a9911f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-14-api-endpoint.md\", \"id\": \"0cf7ef3515c36d5b\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": 